#     - Parser: the `extern type` path branches on `=`. No `=` keeps the opaque `ExternBody`; `= struct { … }`
#       reuses `parse_fields` and wraps them in a new `ExternStructBody`, rejecting methods/consts/interfaces
#       ("an extern struct declares only fields"). A non-struct body after `=` is a clear parse error.
#     - AST: new `ExternStructBody { fields }` beside `ExternBody`, added to the `TypeBody()` union; the new
