#       extern struct (a validator pass reports a bad field); a shared `extern_named_body_ok` widens
#       `extern_type_ok` to admit an extern struct by value and a `ref T` out-pointer whose inner is extern-
#       admissible; field-projection and struct-literal construction gained the `ExternStructBody` arm.
#     - Codegen: `emit_extern_struct_typedef` emits the `StructBody` typedef MINUS the `tk_struct_hdr __hdr`
#       header line — the layout is byte-identical to the foreign C struct; a forward `typedef struct` is
#       emitted for pointer fields. The `ref T`→C-pointer crossing rides the existing `&local` path.
